  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "He has a broad shoulder and a thin waist. His image is blurred, but his skin is covered in rainbow colors, and ancient totems of every description are carved on it. His purple hair flutters, and flames seem to burn within his double pupil eyes.",
      "chapters": [
        597
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The inheritance holds a trace of his will. Giant Sun Immortal Venerable had already modified that test so mortals could endure it. He is the progenitor of strength path and the creator of transformation path, the fiercest venerable out of the ten, able to transform into countless fierce beasts and to revive from a drop of blood.",
      "chapters": [
        597
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_giant_sun_immortal_venerable",
        "path_strength"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "From within the electricity, his bronze colored body stays intact and shines brightly. His muscles are like stone blocks. Totems on his body are like living beings, with fierce beasts roaming on his body. He expands with the wind and becomes a giant as tall as heaven and earth.",
      "chapters": [
        597
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "primordial-ash-owl",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Legend at the absolute ice battlefield in the northernmost part of Northern Plains says he fought strong enemies there, destroyed the place, and created an area of void. After the battle he turned into the immemorial desolate beast ice phoenix and breathed absolute profound ice to freeze and restore it.",
      "chapters": [
        683
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "battle-and-restoration",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_northern_plains"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fairy Li Shan says that as creator of that icy plain he imprinted the true meaning of strength path and transformation path in that land. Even after rank nine venerables perish, their main killer move is imprinted in heaven and earth as a kind of heavenly tribulation and earthly calamity. A strength path or transformation path Gu Master who ascends to immortal there may evoke that true meaning.",
      "chapters": [
        686
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "true-meaning-imprint",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fairy_li_shan",
        "path_strength",
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "During Fang Yuan’s first earthly calamity, Reckless Savage’s true meaning took over a large portion of it from heaven’s will, forming iron crown eagles, ruin bats, and other threats. Only the snow monsters remained heaven’s will’s own, and Reckless Savage’s true meaning weakened their danger by a large degree.",
      "chapters": [
        1085
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "true-meaning-imprint",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Heavenly Court Gu Immortal inside Embroidered Tower says that its needle move once struck Reckless Savage Demon Venerable during his rampage into Heavenly Court, and that he freed himself only by discarding three bloody skins.",
      "chapters": [
        1010
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "heavenly-court-rampage",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "house_embroidered_tower"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Historical records state that he could transform into countless things and change dao marks at will, so a lightning wolf form could use lightning path killer moves and a swamp crab form could use earth path killer moves without other dao marks weakening them. After Reckless Savage Demon Venerable died, that method was not passed down.",
      "chapters": [
        1041
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "During Reckless Savage Demon Venerable’s era, humans and variant humans fought for a hundred days and nights in Western Desert. That battlefield later became myriad statue desert, known throughout Western Desert’s Gu Immortal world. Transformation path was the mainstream path then. Thousand Transformations Ancestor relies on a Reckless Savage true inheritance.",
      "chapters": [
        1398
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "western-desert-battlefield",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_western_desert",
        "path_transformation",
        "char_thousand_transformations_ancestor",
        "inh_reckless_savage_true_inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Longevity Heaven holds true inheritances of several Demon Venerables. Reckless Savage and Limitless were Northern Plains men, and Longevity Heaven holds intel of their attack on Heavenly Court.",
      "chapters": [
        1710
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "northern-plains-origin",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_longevity_heaven",
        "reg_northern_plains"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He wears an extremely wide beast skin cape sewn from human skins. The cape suits a large physique. On an ordinary person a large portion would drag on the ground. His thighs are sturdy. His arms are muscular and well-defined. Each time he killed a rank eight enemy, he peeled their skin and sewed it onto the cape.",
      "chapters": [
        1956
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "trophy-cape",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
